OVITO (Open Visualization Tool) is a scientific visualization and
analysis program for atomistic, molecular and other particle-based
simulation data, e.g. from LAMMPS, GROMACS or SPH codes.  It reads
many file formats, offers a modifier pipeline for analysis (structure
identification, cluster analysis, dislocation analysis, Voronoi
tessellation, ...), and renders images and movies with its real-time
renderer, which uses Metal on macOS and Vulkan elsewhere through Qt's
RHI.

This is the open-source code base of OVITO Basic; the Python module
and the Pro-only features are not included.
